  m_Name: 1200 orang laut
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: "Rickshaws and Bullock Carts \u2013 1800s "
  info: "In the 19th century, rickshaws and bullock carts were the primary modes
    of transport for early settlers and traders in Singapore. Rickshaw pullers carried
    passengers through bustling streets, while bullock carts were used to transport
    goods. These traditional vehicles symbolized Singapore\u2019s early economic
    activities and urban development.  "
